--- !u!114 &-6668057430241694526
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. Select the <b>Play</b> button at the top of the <b>Unity
      Editor</b>. A new robot card appears in the <b>Dashboard</b> left panel. Cards
      are sorted alphabetically and the total robot count increases by <b>1</b>.\n\n2.
      In the <b>Dashboard</b> left panel, click the new robot\u2019s card. The selected
      card becomes highlighted. The <b>right panel</b> displays detailed data about
      the selected robot and the <b>camera</b> smoothly transitions to follow the
      robot in the scene."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-5680823090892696129
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Your robot supports both manual and autonomous control modes.
      In manual mode, you can control the robot using the keyboard. In autonomous
      mode, the robot navigates between predefined warehouse waypoints on its own.\nIn
      this step, you\u2019ll test both control modes and observe the behavior change
      in real time.\n"
--- !u!114 &-5212420604749216343
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. Activate <b>Play</b> mode again.\n\n<b>Note:</b> We recommend
      expanding the Game window for a better view of the application menus.\n\n2.
      In the <b>Dashboard</b>, select the <b>Variant Switcher</b> button. The robot\u2019s
      visual model updates to the next variant.\n\n3. Use the <b>Arm Range</b> slider
      to confirm the animation still works with the new variant.\n\n4. In the <b>Dashboard</b>
      left panel, select the card for your new robot.\n\n5. In the <b>Project</b>
      window, go to <b>Assets > Warehouse > RobotData</b>.\n\n6.  Select the <b>Robot
      Data</b> ScriptableObject linked to your robot.\n\n7. In the <b>Inspector</b>,
      set <b>Battery</b> to <b>50</b>. The UI shows <b>50%</b> and enters a <b>Warning
      (yellow)</b> state.\n\n8. Change <b>Battery</b> to <b>20</b>. The UI updates
      to <b>20%</b> and shows a <b>Critical (red)</b> status.\n\n9. In the <b>Inspector</b>,
      set <b>Health</b> to <b>0</b>. The robot enters <b>DEAD</b> status and the
      card displays <b>Critical styling</b> in the Dashboard. Movement commands are
      ignored while the robot is in this state."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
